WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.010
Stage twenty-three: the next pair.

2
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:11.195
Threshold crossed, red inspection, or retired by Garmin: Camille's Crête Pro is done.

3
00:00:11.295 --> 00:00:12.953
What replaces it?

4
00:00:13.803 --> 00:00:19.578
Every pair has a spec sheet. Each value carries its source: lab, brand, or you.

5
00:00:19.678 --> 00:00:24.515
Measurement wins: six millimetres of drop claimed, nearly nine measured.

6
00:00:24.615 --> 00:00:29.068
Never a neighbouring model's value, and nothing without your approval.

7
00:00:29.918 --> 00:00:35.011
After a run, /log records comfort, a blister, a tight toe box.

8
00:00:35.111 --> 00:00:38.710
At retirement, a verdict: would you buy it again?

9
00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:41.855
Never in place of a reported pain.

10
00:00:42.705 --> 00:00:48.459
The usage profile shows what the pair did: type of ground, climb, long runs.

11
00:00:48.559 --> 00:00:52.606
Stride compared at a comparable pace, three runs minimum.

12
00:00:52.706 --> 00:00:57.799
Pain: correlation, not causation, no rate under five episodes.

13
00:00:58.649 --> 00:01:04.168
The engine derives target ranges: drop, stack, softness, lugs, width.

14
00:01:04.268 --> 00:01:08.636
Each with its rule, evidence and references. Never a brand.

15
00:01:08.736 --> 00:01:11.994
Achilles history? The drop is never lowered.

16
00:01:12.844 --> 00:01:20.433
Type /shoes. Continuity first: the current version of the model that suited you, compared with the old one.

17
00:01:20.533 --> 00:01:25.199
Otherwise, three to five models found online, every value sourced.

18
00:01:25.299 --> 00:01:28.215
The medical agent can rule one out.

19
00:01:29.065 --> 00:01:32.024
Try them in store: comfort decides.

20
00:01:32.124 --> 00:01:37.558
Break them in over thirty to fifty kilometres; keep two pairs in rotation.

21
00:01:37.658 --> 00:01:43.476
No purchase, no price, no affiliate link, no promise of injury prevention.

22
00:01:46.026 --> 00:01:50.287
To go further: the “Choosing your shoes” documentation page.
